ate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I originally made this change to avoid ending up with one extra pixel compared to what `style.get_minimum_size()` returns, since each margin could be rounded up individually. But I agree this causes confusion, margins should be usable individually without additional operations, and `get_minimum_size()` should consistently equal (side_left + side_right).\r\n\r\nI’ll make sure all margins multiplied by `EDSCALE` are rounded properly, since they’re floats and can otherwise lead to inconsistent results.\r\n\r\nEdit: Also AFAIR i have changed both to use ceil and maybe i have tested with flooring right margin and it also was solving the issue and i forgot to revert it back to ceil, but to avoid the confusion I will solve it in `editor_theme_manager.cpp` instead.","created_at":"2025-09-22T13:02:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T13:23:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110527#discussion_r2368279737","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2368279737"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110527#discussion_r2368279737"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2368279737/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket"